n JT, Jeffreys AJ</person-group><article-title>Notes on the definition and nomenclature of tandemly repetitive DNA sequences</article-title><source>DNA fingerprinting: State of the science</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>Basel: Birkhauser Verlag</publisher-name><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>28</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>T&#x000f3;th</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>G&#x000e1;sp&#x000e1;ri</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Jurka</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Microsatellites in different eukaryotic genomes: Survey and analysis</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>967</fpage><lpage>981</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1101/gr.10.7.967</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10899146</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Rossi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Wincker</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ravel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Blaineau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pages</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bastien</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><article-title>Structural organisation of microsatellite families in the <italic>Leishmania</italic> genome and polymorphisms at two (CA)n loci</article-title><source>Mol Biochem Parasitol</source><year>1994</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>282</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0166-6851(94)90078-7</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7969268</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ivens</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Peacock</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Worthey</surname><g